    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305-a1">

                <pb facs="0632" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg522"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    45.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Firmin to Mr.
                            Douglass.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bureau of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: The Government is informed that
                    many persons are at this moment refugees in the legations or consulates
                    established in this city, because the law pursues (<hi rendition="#italic">la
                        justice recherche</hi>) those whom public clamor has denounced as having
                    committed common law crimes and misdemeanors during the course of the last civil
                    strife in the country.</p>
                <p>If this information is correct, I pray you to be pleased to furnish me with a
                    list of the persons to whom you have accorded the protection of your flag.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Firmin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
